WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.130 --> 00:00:03.449
Speaker 1: Listen, I want to keep talking
about the Twitter files.

00:00:03.449 --> 00:00:06.290
I know that many of you are following the
Twitter files.

00:00:06.290 --> 00:00:09.599
And I also want to make very clear what it
is.

00:00:09.599 --> 00:00:11.000
It's right wing bait.

00:00:11.000 --> 00:00:12.000
That's what it is.

00:00:12.000 --> 00:00:16.119
It's meant to get people who don't really
know what's going on or who don't actually

00:00:16.119 --> 00:00:21.510
read the Twitter files threads or who simply
are looking for something to be outraged.

00:00:21.510 --> 00:00:26.490
About to be outraged and to say we all the
stuff that we said was happening was happening

00:00:26.490 --> 00:00:30.000
and people need to go to jail or something
bad needs to happen.

00:00:30.000 --> 00:00:31.670
So let's take a step back.

00:00:31.670 --> 00:00:37.239
We have now seen at least three releases of
the Twitter files.

00:00:37.239 --> 00:00:45.870
The Twitter files are supposedly exclusive
stories given to Matt Taibbi and Bari Weiss

00:00:45.870 --> 00:00:53.059
to tweet about exposing everything that happened
at Twitter.

00:00:53.059 --> 00:00:55.469
And it turns out that really not that much
happened.

00:00:55.469 --> 00:01:02.149
For example, we learned that there was an
effort being made in 2020 by the Biden campaign

00:01:02.149 --> 00:01:08.080
to have explicit images of Hunter Biden removed
from the platform.

00:01:08.080 --> 00:01:12.430
Now, they were nude, explicit images of Hunter
published without his consent.

00:01:12.430 --> 00:01:16.930
That's not allowed on Twitter per their own
terms of service.

00:01:16.930 --> 00:01:21.600
And it's also against the law in most states
to publish such images.

00:01:21.600 --> 00:01:27.540
And it was framed by some on the right as
the Biden administration is censoring content

00:01:27.540 --> 00:01:28.690
on Twitter.

00:01:28.690 --> 00:01:33.250
Well, there was no Biden administration at
the time, so crossed that piece off.

00:01:33.250 --> 00:01:34.860
And they're not really censoring anything.

00:01:34.860 --> 00:01:39.280
They're asking that content in violation of
Twitter's own policies be removed.

00:01:39.280 --> 00:01:46.160
It wasn't really a bombshell as the Twitter
files have continued coming out, more and

00:01:46.160 --> 00:01:50.659
more clear thinking individuals have realized
what many of us realized pretty quickly.

00:01:50.659 --> 00:01:55.380
Charlie Wurtzel writes about this in The Atlantic
in an article I encourage you to read called

00:01:55.380 --> 00:01:58.570
Elon Musk's Twitter Files Are Bait.

00:01:58.570 --> 00:02:02.800
He doesn't actually want transparency on the
social media platform.

00:02:02.800 --> 00:02:05.400
And this is, of course, absolutely correct.

00:02:05.400 --> 00:02:12.879
The Twitter files expose no crimes that that
are clearly related to the actions Twitter

00:02:12.879 --> 00:02:13.879
took.

00:02:13.879 --> 00:02:17.290
I'm going to get to perjury in a second, and
I have no interest in hiding anything from

00:02:17.290 --> 00:02:18.290
you.

00:02:18.290 --> 00:02:21.090
The emails I get, David, you're hiding this
and that.

00:02:21.090 --> 00:02:22.879
I'm just a guy in a room with a microphone.

00:02:22.879 --> 00:02:24.379
I'm not hiding anything.

00:02:24.379 --> 00:02:25.379
We'll get to perjury.

00:02:25.379 --> 00:02:30.380
But the Twitter files expose no crimes with
regard to Twitter's actions, and they don't

00:02:30.380 --> 00:02:33.350
even expose violations of Twitter's own terms
of service.

00:02:33.350 --> 00:02:39.209
Twitter's own terms of service, if you want
to read them, include a process for communicating

00:02:39.209 --> 00:02:40.209
content.

00:02:40.209 --> 00:02:43.510
That content is violating Twitter's terms
of service.

00:02:43.510 --> 00:02:48.569
It includes these very general catch that
these social media platforms can, at the end

00:02:48.569 --> 00:02:52.950
of the day, decide to moderate content however
the hell they want.

00:02:52.950 --> 00:02:58.290
As long as they're not doing something like
saying we don't allow Christians to post,

00:02:58.290 --> 00:03:00.659
that would be against the law.

00:03:00.659 --> 00:03:05.220
But beyond that, all of these platforms can
do this and it's in their terms of service.

00:03:05.220 --> 00:03:08.879
Now, you can say you disagree with it, okay,
but it's in their terms of service.

00:03:08.879 --> 00:03:14.640
So the point here is the Twitter files expose
no crimes and no violations of Twitter's own

00:03:14.640 --> 00:03:15.909
terms of service.

00:03:15.909 --> 00:03:21.930
They are intended to play to the right wing
persecution complex.

00:03:21.930 --> 00:03:23.629
We're being censored.

00:03:23.629 --> 00:03:25.060
We're being silenced.

00:03:25.060 --> 00:03:31.980
We're not allowed to give the alternative
perspectives on COVID or on drinking urine

00:03:31.980 --> 00:03:34.599
neuron, whatever it is that they want to do.

00:03:34.599 --> 00:03:41.280
When private businesses tell you, Here's what
we're doing in our terms of service and you

00:03:41.280 --> 00:03:46.650
accept and then they do it, there isn't very
much to talk about.

00:03:46.650 --> 00:03:52.690
At worst, what we're learning is something
we knew, which is Twitter does what Fox News

00:03:52.690 --> 00:03:53.769
does, right.

00:03:53.769 --> 00:04:01.400
If you want to accept the most heavy argument
that could be made, which I don't believe

00:04:01.400 --> 00:04:08.769
is actually defensible based on it, but what
would be Twitter is crafting a partizan message,

00:04:08.769 --> 00:04:13.689
a message in through their moderation and
decisions.

00:04:13.689 --> 00:04:17.420
Well, that's what Fox News does, the difference
being.

00:04:17.420 --> 00:04:20.820
Twitter is a platform on which everybody gets
to post, at least in principle.

00:04:20.820 --> 00:04:29.060
Fox News is broadcasting out one way no connection
between the Biden campaign and the suspension

00:04:29.060 --> 00:04:33.540
of Donald Trump on Twitter, which was a big
thing that they had their hopes very high

00:04:33.540 --> 00:04:34.540
for.

00:04:34.540 --> 00:04:41.830
The most interesting part out of all of this
to me is the part of the files that say the

00:04:41.830 --> 00:04:49.320
Trump administration not campaign apparently
had the exact type of access to Twitter moderation,

00:04:49.320 --> 00:04:51.340
meaning they had email addresses, they could
email.

00:04:51.340 --> 00:04:59.000
So part of the controversy is that the Biden
campaign, rather than reporting tweets, the

00:04:59.000 --> 00:05:03.900
way you and I have to had email addresses
of people at Twitter that they could email

00:05:03.900 --> 00:05:04.960
and say, hey, take a look at this.

00:05:04.960 --> 00:05:05.979
Take a look at that.

00:05:05.979 --> 00:05:07.530
You could argue that that's wrong.

00:05:07.530 --> 00:05:11.539
You could argue the Biden campaign should
have had to use the same system we all have

00:05:11.539 --> 00:05:12.979
to use to report tweets.

00:05:12.979 --> 00:05:13.979
Fine.

00:05:13.979 --> 00:05:20.330
But the Twitter files also say that the Trump
administration had the very same email access.

00:05:20.330 --> 00:05:23.570
Conservatives are silent about that part.

00:05:23.570 --> 00:05:24.740
Okay.

00:05:24.740 --> 00:05:29.880
Let's now talk about maybe maybe the one part
that maybe is something.

00:05:29.880 --> 00:05:34.039
And I'm getting emails from people saying,
David, you won't talk about this.

00:05:34.039 --> 00:05:37.430
Listen up, folks, buckle in because I'm talking
about it.

00:05:37.430 --> 00:05:42.789
The one thing I can maybe find that that would
be under the route, the umbrella of what we

00:05:42.789 --> 00:05:49.850
would call criminal, is that there are now
allegations that Jack Dorsey perjured himself,

00:05:49.850 --> 00:05:55.979
former CEO of Twitter, one of the instrumental
early people, Jack Dorsey said to Congress

00:05:55.979 --> 00:05:57.639
under oath.

00:05:57.639 --> 00:06:00.669
Twitter isn't shadow banning people.

00:06:00.669 --> 00:06:07.300
According to the Twitter files, Twitter was
shadow banning people, and thus that is perjury

00:06:07.300 --> 00:06:09.990
because Jack lied under oath.

00:06:09.990 --> 00:06:12.650
Let's take a look at the clip from that hearing
years ago.

00:06:12.650 --> 00:06:17.680
Speaker 3: I want to read a few quotes about
Twitter's practices, and I just want you to

00:06:17.680 --> 00:06:19.510
tell me if they're true or not.

00:06:19.510 --> 00:06:20.510
Please.

00:06:20.510 --> 00:06:24.070
Social media is being rigged to censor conservatives.

00:06:24.070 --> 00:06:26.250
Is that true of Twitter?

00:06:26.250 --> 00:06:27.600
No.

00:06:27.600 --> 00:06:29.460
I don't know what Twitter is up to.

00:06:29.460 --> 00:06:34.080
It sure looks like to me that they're censoring
people and they ought to stop it.

00:06:34.080 --> 00:06:35.949
Are you censoring people?

00:06:35.949 --> 00:06:37.190
No.

00:06:37.190 --> 00:06:39.690
Twitter Shadow Banning Prominent Republicans.

00:06:39.690 --> 00:06:42.090
Speaker 2: Bad.

00:06:42.090 --> 00:06:43.090
Is that true?

00:06:43.090 --> 00:06:44.090
No.

00:06:44.090 --> 00:06:45.090
Speaker 1: Okay.

00:06:45.090 --> 00:06:49.610
So Jack Dorsey said we are not shadow banning
people.

00:06:49.610 --> 00:06:54.310
And it appears based on some of the stuff
that's been released that that Twitter was.

00:06:54.310 --> 00:06:56.700
So listen very carefully here.

00:06:56.700 --> 00:07:03.080
If Jack Dorsey perjured himself and you can
prove it, throw the book at him, prosecute

00:07:03.080 --> 00:07:04.229
him, do it.

00:07:04.229 --> 00:07:09.930
I don't care if you can prove that the shadow
banned screenshots released in the Twitter

00:07:09.930 --> 00:07:17.750
files are real and that Jack Dorsey knew that
there was shadow banning going on when he

00:07:17.750 --> 00:07:18.750
testified.

00:07:18.750 --> 00:07:19.750
Right?

00:07:19.750 --> 00:07:20.750
Because that's part of it.

00:07:20.750 --> 00:07:21.750
Perjury.

00:07:21.750 --> 00:07:23.580
Did you know that you were telling a lie?

00:07:23.580 --> 00:07:26.879
If you can prove those two points, then go
ahead and prosecute him.

00:07:26.879 --> 00:07:32.979
I do want to remind you, however, Republicans
spent three years during the Mueller probe

00:07:32.979 --> 00:07:38.500
saying lying to Congress and lying to the
FBI, that's all you can get.

00:07:38.500 --> 00:07:40.930
What about the underlying crimes?

00:07:40.930 --> 00:07:43.590
What about the collusion with Russia?

00:07:43.590 --> 00:07:45.599
What about this, that or the other thing?

00:07:45.599 --> 00:07:46.930
Financial crimes.

00:07:46.930 --> 00:07:49.590
All you've got is lying under oath.

00:07:49.590 --> 00:07:53.039
That's the only thing that's politically targeted.

00:07:53.039 --> 00:07:55.600
Those when all you have is lying.

00:07:55.600 --> 00:07:58.830
Those are politically targeted prosecutions
of Trump people.

00:07:58.830 --> 00:08:01.080
We shouldn't even be worried about that.

00:08:01.080 --> 00:08:02.080
Well.

00:08:02.080 --> 00:08:05.919
If you were saying that during the Mueller
probe, then maybe you should be saying the

00:08:05.919 --> 00:08:07.699
same thing here.

00:08:07.699 --> 00:08:09.380
Notice I'm not saying that.

00:08:09.380 --> 00:08:12.180
I'm saying if he perjured himself, go after
him.

00:08:12.180 --> 00:08:17.280
It doesn't relate to the type of criminality
that they've been alleging.

00:08:17.280 --> 00:08:18.280
Twitter engaged in.

00:08:18.280 --> 00:08:21.020
This is just a guy who maybe lied.

00:08:21.020 --> 00:08:24.030
Go after him for it, by all means.

00:08:24.030 --> 00:08:27.930
But remember that you all were the ones saying
during the Mueller probe, when all you've

00:08:27.930 --> 00:09:36.110
got is lying, you know, you've really 
got nothing.

